From 7d4bd239990625ccc9f77e1258d5304b8c708c4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Tomaszewski <scottTomaszewski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:15:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] fix(SC-479): the host pin's anchoring stop goes on the
 host's embeds, not its scroller

With scroll anchoring off on the whole host scroller, a height change above the viewport during the
pin moved on-screen text instead of being compensated: a write adding or removing a tracker row while
the reader is below the embed shifted the text 110 px (stock: 0). The rule now targets
.internal-embed under the pinned scroller, so only the collapsing embed is excluded as an anchor
(measured: the end/in geometries still hold, every shift case 0 px). Header rewritten to match.
---
 src/framework/host/previewScrollPin.ts      | 42 ++++++++++++++-------
 test/dom/framework/previewScrollPin.test.ts | 15 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

